  {
    "event": {
      "address": "90 Lots Road, London SW10 0QD",
      "all_day": false,
      "category": "music",
      "dedupe_key": "peter-king-memorial-sax-summit-mornington-lockett-tommaso-starace-karen-sharp-donovan-haffner-rob-barron-trio|2026-11-14|606-club",
      "description": "Intro by Steve Rubie: One of the finest saxophonists the UK has ever produced Peter King was unquestionably a genius (an overused word but in his case absolutely appropriate). An inspiration to 4 generations of saxophonists (including me!) every gig was an event. It’s an honour to keep his memory alive with this annual LJF gig. Tonight we will be hosting an evening dedicated to one of the UK's musical giants, the brilliant alto sax player Peter King, who led our Sax Summit for many years before he sadly passed away in 2020. This remarkable gig features a breathtaking 4-sax front line, each with their own unique sound and approach. A regular at the Club Mornington Lockett, who performed here with Peter for many years, is one of the UK’s leading tenor sax players. A former member of the Ronnie Scott quintet he has worked with singer Sarah Jane Morris and the Tracey’s - Stan and Clark - and was the driving force behind the brilliant “Celebrating the Jazz Couriers” quintet. He can be seen regularly at the Club with his own group. Alto saxophonist Tommaso Starace has performed at many of the top European jazz clubs and festivals and his fluent, hard-bop influenced playing has been heard with a notable cohort of international jazz musicians, including Billy Cobham, David Liebman and Kenny Wheeler. With 11 albums to his name (the latest just launched at the Club) it’s a pleasure to welcome this impressive, highly respected, player to the Sax Summit this evening. A prominent figure on the UK Jazz scene since moving to London in 2000, the multi-Award-winning Karen Sharp is universally admired for her melodic yet distinctive, saxophone playing. A member of the iconic UK trumpet player Humphrey Lyttelton's band, she’s since appeared as a soloist with an impressive array of high-profile artists, including the likes of US stars Scott Hamilton, Warren Vache and Bucky Pizzarelli as well as with larger ensembles such as the Guy Barker Big Band at the BBC Proms and Ronnie Scott's Jazz Orchestra. A nominee in the Rising Star category of the US Downbeat Critics Poll, she has won the British Jazz Award on several occasions. Up-and-coming alto saxophonist Donovan Haffner already has, in his burgeoning career, won the 'Breakthrough Act of the Year' category at the Jazz FM Awards 2026, the 'Martin Hummel' Parliamentary Jazz Award 2026 & ‘Jazz Newcomer’ Award 2025 and Tina May Young Musician Award 2026. His debut album “Alleviate” has further confirmed his tremendous ability and talent. This stunning lineup will be accompanied by one of the UK’s leading jazz pianists Rob Barron (Al Jarreau, Patti Austin, Marlena Shaw) & his trio featuring Calum Gourlay -bass & Mark Taylor -drums. “Lockett…plays with tremendous fluency and drive” Evening Standard; “Starace is on fire” Bebop Spoken Here; “Sharp loves melody, whether composed or improvised, as reflected in her relaxed and natural phrasing” Downbeat; “'Alleviate’ is an absolutely awesome debut… [Donovan] has blossomed into a really special musician” Tony Minvielle, Jazz FM/One Jazz Photo, Mornington Lockett by Tatiana Gorilovsky",
      "ends_at": null,
      "image_url": "https://www.606club.co.uk/media/cache/event_large/uploads/events/peter-king-memorial-sax-summit-mornington-lockett-tommaso-starace-karen-sharp-donovan-haffner-the-rob-barron-trio-24866.png",
      "lat": null,
      "lng": null,
      "price": {
        "currency": "GBP",
        "is_free": false,
        "max": "25.00",
        "min": "25.00"
      },
      "starts_at": "2026-11-14T21:00:00Z",
      "tags": [
        "jazz"
      ],
      "title": "Peter King Memorial Sax Summit: Mornington Lockett, Tommaso Starace, Karen Sharp, Donovan Haffner & the Rob Barron Trio",
      "url": "https://www.606club.co.uk/events/view/peter-king-memorial-sax-summit-mornington-lockett-tommaso-starace-karen-sharp-donovan-haffner-the-rob-barron-trio/",
      "venue_name": "606 Club"
    },
    "source_event_id": "peter-king-memorial-sax-summit-mornington-lockett-tommaso-starace-karen-sharp-donovan-haffner-the-rob-barron-trio",
    "when": "Saturday 14 th November 2026 - 9:00 pm"
  },
  {
    "event": {
      "address": "90 Lots Road, London SW10 0QD",
      "all_day": false,
      "category": "music",
      "dedupe_key": "world-heart-beat-music-academy-julian-joseph-jazz-academy-present-together-we-go-forward|2026-11-15|606-club",
      "description": "The 606 Club has always looked to the future generations of musicians and as part of that philosophy has good working relationships with a number of Schools and Academies. This afternoon we are very pleased to welcome two institutions particularly close to the 606 Club, World Heart Beat Music Academy and the Julian Joseph Academy who will be jointly presenting their programme “Together We Go Forward”. This is how they describe what they do and what to expect from the show: Long standing partners in music education, the World Heart Beat and Julian Joseph Jazz Academies join together to showcase the talents of their students at the 606 for this special performance. World Heart Beat’s jazz curriculum is spearheaded by the exemplary work of internationally renowned British jazz musicians such as Tony Kofi and Byron Wallen, as well benefitting from the energy of the new generation of jazz musicians including pianist Ayo Vincent, trombonist Wilf Diamond, and vocalist Ava Joseph. World Heart Beat students are exposed to specialist jazz programmes at Julian Joseph Jazz Academy, whilst JJJA students are given opportunity at World Heart Beat to expand their experience with opportunities in recording and live performance, as well as extra development in classical music, orchestra, Indian tabla, Latin and playing in the 51st State Big Band, performances and mentoring opportunities. In addition, World Heart Beat recently opened a state of the art venue in their new Embassy Gardens location, equipped with the innovative and groundbreaking d&b Soundscape technology which allows students to further push their musical boundaries. This afternoon, expect a wonderful programme where young, soulful, and talented jazz musicians from the two academies play a mix of standards and jazz standards. Previous alumni of both academies have gone on to win Jazz FM Awards, Berklee scholarships, and the BBC Young Jazz Musician of The Year, so if you want to be the first catch the next generation of jazz musicians, this is most definitely the gig for you!",
      "ends_at": null,
      "image_url": "https://www.606club.co.uk/media/cache/event_large/uploads/events/world-heart-beat-music-academy-and-the-julian-joseph-jazz-academy-present-together-we-go-forward-5-33678.jpeg",
      "lat": null,
      "lng": null,
